class:: Tempogram
summary:: Autocorrelation tempo evidence
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3, Classes/FourierTempogram, Classes/BeatHistogram, Classes/Tempo

description::
Mean-centered onset history is autocorrelated through a zero-padded FFT. Correlation at lag 60*featureRate/BPM is linearly interpolated and normalized by overlap energy; negative correlation is zeroed.

The periodicity-analysis source is Grosche, Müller and Kurth (2010), link::https://resources.mpi-inf.mpg.de/MIR/tempogramtoolbox/2010_GroscheMuellerKurth_TempogramCyclic_ICASSP.pdf::. MIRa uses trailing absolute-BPM windows and an original causal tracker; it does not implement cyclic tempo folding or claim equivalence with the paper. Output begins after the requested warmup and sufficient periods, and is held between analyses. Silence clears evidence as it leaves the trailing window. Tempo ambiguities, syncopation, sparse events and changing meter remain limitations. Vanilla BeatTrack also estimates pulse timing; MIRa exposes the evidence distribution, alternative tempi and explicit continuity controls.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: in
Nonnegative control-rate onset strength, such as Onsets2 novelty. Audio-rate input is rejected.

argument:: minBPM
Lowest tempo in BPM, at least 20; literal at construction.

argument:: maxBPM
Highest tempo in BPM, greater than minBPM and at most 600; literal at construction.

argument:: numBins
Literal number of linearly spaced BPM bins, 8–512. Defaults to 128 for vectors and 271 for scalar estimates.

argument:: windowTime
Trailing history in seconds. Rhythm analysis accepts 0.5–16, default 6; onset/tempo statistics accept 0.05–60, default 4.

argument:: hopTime
Analysis interval in seconds, 0.02–2, default 0.1; rounded to a whole number of pooled feature frames.

argument:: featureRate
Requested onset-envelope rate, 20–200 Hz, default 100. Maximum pooling spans a rounded number of server control blocks; the actual rate is used in all timing calculations.

argument:: normalize
Positive selects normalized evidence; zero returns raw correlation per overlap sample or raw Fourier magnitude. Histogram normalization makes its sum one.

method:: bpms
Returns the linear BPM grid for matching minBPM, maxBPM and numBins arguments.

returns::
An Array of numBins tempo strengths; normalized values are 0–1.

examples::
Tempogram computes cyclic autocorrelation tempo evidence across a wide BPM lag spectrum ($40 \dots 240$ BPM). In this example, it analyzes an acoustic drum groove: peak tempo evidence modulates an auxiliary poly-metric comb delay network that locks into sympathetic resonance with the drum meter. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.heatmap:: displays the real-time autocorrelation tempogram.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 48);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var tempoGram = Tempogram.kr(onset[1], minBPM: 40, maxBPM: 240, numBins: 48, windowTime: 4.0, hopTime: 0.1);
        var peakEnergy = tempoGram.inject(0, { |maxVal, val| maxVal.max(val) }).lag(0.05);

        // Sympathetic metric comb resonator
        var comb = CombC.ar(source, 0.5, 60.0 / 120.0 * 0.5, 0.4) * peakEnergy.clip(0, 1) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + comb;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, tempoGram.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.heatmap("Tempogram", ~miraBus, 48);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
